WEBVTT

00:25.791 --> 00:28.881
Well then, what can I do?

00:30.301 --> 00:33.471
How can I protect my country from these fools?

00:37.301 --> 00:40.141
As a reward for saving the prince,

00:40.221 --> 00:43.021
the king presents you with 50 pounds of silver.

00:43.101 --> 00:44.941
Accept it with gratitude.

00:46.601 --> 00:51.401
I heard that you fought hard to save Canute.

00:51.481 --> 00:53.111
Accept my gratitude.

00:53.941 --> 00:56.781
Yes, Your Highness. Thank you for your reward.

00:59.451 --> 01:04.751
I have high expectations of you
in our battle to subjugate Wales.

01:07.711 --> 01:11.631
It appears that sly old fox has noticed.

01:14.131 --> 01:17.761
Your Highness, with all due respect,

01:22.811 --> 01:25.311
are you sure that your plan to subjugate Wales

01:27.601 --> 01:31.191
is the best decision?

03:05.081 --> 03:06.741
END OF THE PROLOGUE

03:06.831 --> 03:11.041
I believe the campaign to subjugate Wales next spring
will prove to be a fruitless battle for our army.

03:12.501 --> 03:14.461
Please, reconsider the matter.

03:15.461 --> 03:19.761
Askeladd, you said you weren't going
to stir up trouble for now.

03:19.841 --> 03:21.881
So that's Askeladd?

03:21.971 --> 03:24.681
I can't believe he objected
to the king's plan in front of him.

03:24.761 --> 03:27.311
Sorry, Your Highness.

03:29.521 --> 03:34.981
When it comes to Wales, I'm not going to back down.

03:36.941 --> 03:38.941
Explain your reasoning.

03:40.071 --> 03:41.611
Thank you.

03:43.361 --> 03:48.741
First, we've been fighting the English for 10 years.

03:49.951 --> 03:54.921
We should be focusing on recovery
for our people and our land right now.

03:55.001 --> 03:58.251
Another reason is that
the terrain in Wales is perilous,

03:58.341 --> 04:00.801
and as a result, the land is infertile.

04:01.921 --> 04:05.721
Attacking Wales would be like whipping our horses

04:05.801 --> 04:09.101
to make them jump off a cliff
just to catch a single rabbit.

04:10.101 --> 04:14.941
To put it simply, conquering Wales
isn't worth the cost.

04:16.731 --> 04:17.611
He's right.

04:17.691 --> 04:19.321
I'm glad he said it.

04:20.651 --> 04:22.491
He's good at talking.

04:23.491 --> 04:25.201
This isn't a conquest.

04:25.281 --> 04:28.411
The point is that we can't ignore those
who show disrespect for the king.

04:28.491 --> 04:29.791
Don't get the wrong idea.

04:29.871 --> 04:32.581
If that's what you're worried about,

04:33.911 --> 04:36.631
please, let me be your messenger.

04:36.711 --> 04:41.261
Allow me to show you that
I can persuade the people of Wales.

04:43.551 --> 04:48.261
Are you telling me, the king,
to show courtesy towards them?

04:48.351 --> 04:52.141
To the country you just called "a rabbit"?

04:52.221 --> 04:54.311
If you show courtesy,

04:54.391 --> 04:58.611
then they will understand your generosity.

04:58.691 --> 05:01.071
Please, listen to my entreaty.

05:13.041 --> 05:14.081
Is he going to kill him?

05:26.381 --> 05:29.141
This is how a loyal vassal should act.

05:30.351 --> 05:34.221
The greatest treasure anyone could ever
offer a king is words of advice.

05:34.311 --> 05:38.981
My army is filled with loyal
and brave men like this man.

05:39.691 --> 05:41.521
I am unworthy of your praise.

05:42.781 --> 05:44.321
How boring.

05:47.991 --> 05:50.621
Please, continue to lend me your aid.

05:57.661 --> 06:00.421
Wales or Canute, choose one.

06:02.461 --> 06:06.551
Honestly, I don't care about Wales.

06:07.631 --> 06:11.051
Give me Canute's head and join me,

06:11.141 --> 06:14.221
then I'll let Wales go free.

06:15.561 --> 06:18.481
I've looked into who you are a bit.

06:18.561 --> 06:21.401
Your mother really was a slave.

06:22.401 --> 06:25.731
I can guess why you're so caught up with Wales.

06:26.781 --> 06:29.491
The only merchandise that Wales produces

06:29.571 --> 06:32.411
is slaves.

06:38.211 --> 06:42.131
What do you think? It still sails.

06:42.211 --> 06:45.381
This is the ship you've always wanted to sail on.

06:45.461 --> 06:47.761
I can finally let you onboard.

06:54.301 --> 06:57.811
You can rest until Mord and the others return.

06:57.891 --> 07:00.271
-Hurry up. Bring it over here.
-Okay.

07:09.441 --> 07:11.361
-Is there still a lot left?
-Yes.

07:18.451 --> 07:20.331
What are you doing? Be careful!

07:41.691 --> 07:43.691
You must be hungry, right?

07:43.771 --> 07:47.231
Give me a minute. I have some good jerky.

07:48.691 --> 07:49.611
Thorfinn.

07:54.071 --> 07:56.781
Thorfinn? Where are you?

07:56.871 --> 07:58.791
Thorfinn?

08:05.041 --> 08:06.421
Thorfinn.

08:22.561 --> 08:24.521
I hate the way your face looks.

08:26.021 --> 08:32.741
I'm not going to let the crown rest
on top of a head like yours.

08:36.111 --> 08:37.701
Did he just say...?

08:38.911 --> 08:41.451
What did you just say?

08:43.501 --> 08:46.631
Are you deaf too, you old man?

08:46.711 --> 08:50.501
I said, how dare an ugly old man like you
wear something shiny?

08:53.051 --> 08:55.431
That's not what the face of a king looks like.

09:01.311 --> 09:02.721
Don't move, guards.

09:03.981 --> 09:06.941
The king is within reach of my sword.

09:11.401 --> 09:13.241
-Is he serious?
-Oh, dear.

09:18.201 --> 09:19.121
Askeladd.

09:20.581 --> 09:22.581
You bastard! King Sweyn is mine.

09:22.661 --> 09:24.001
Don't move, Thorkell!

09:24.081 --> 09:26.921
Askeladd's not acting normal. Don't provoke him.

09:32.631 --> 09:37.181
Put away your sword,
then I'll forgive you for this offense.

09:37.261 --> 09:38.841
Forgive me?

09:38.931 --> 09:41.641
Don't push your luck, you savage.

09:41.721 --> 09:44.851
As punishment for mocking my family and my people,

09:44.931 --> 09:47.231
you deserve to die!

09:47.311 --> 09:49.691
This is my last warning.

09:49.771 --> 09:53.691
Put away your sword, Askeladd.

09:53.781 --> 09:56.111
That's my nickname.

09:56.191 --> 10:00.031
I'll tell you the name my mother gave me.
My real name.

10:01.701 --> 10:05.411
Lucius Artorius Castus.

10:05.501 --> 10:11.591
I am the legitimate king who deserves
to rule over the land of Britannia.

10:15.211 --> 10:17.341
Now. Go!

10:45.541 --> 10:47.201
I feel better now.

10:55.631 --> 10:57.171
All right.

11:04.761 --> 11:07.221
What are you standing there for? Engage!

11:07.311 --> 11:09.021
Engage!

11:10.021 --> 11:12.811
This man is the criminal who murdered the king!

11:12.901 --> 11:14.361
Kill him!

11:18.691 --> 11:20.531
Hey, what's going on?

11:35.921 --> 11:36.881
What?

11:39.171 --> 11:41.381
What's he doing?

11:43.181 --> 11:45.051
What's going on?

11:46.301 --> 11:48.141
What's he doing?

11:48.221 --> 11:50.771
That idiot!

12:04.531 --> 12:05.661
What's wrong?

12:05.741 --> 12:08.291
Who wants to die next? Step up!

12:08.371 --> 12:12.911
The king of Britannia is going to kill you himself!

12:13.001 --> 12:16.421
Don't be afraid! Surround him!

12:22.631 --> 12:23.801
Die!

12:28.431 --> 12:29.641
Hurry up!

12:29.721 --> 12:31.931
-Don't push!
-You too!

12:32.021 --> 12:33.271
Out of my way!

12:33.351 --> 12:35.441
Damn. Out of my way!

12:36.651 --> 12:38.441
Askeladd!

12:44.151 --> 12:45.821
Hold it in, Thorkell.

12:45.911 --> 12:47.821
It's not your turn yet.

12:47.911 --> 12:50.371
I don't care anymore.

12:50.451 --> 12:52.161
He's gone mad.

12:52.251 --> 12:56.251
I hate it when someone steals my prey.

12:56.331 --> 12:59.251
He hasn't gone mad.

12:59.341 --> 13:00.711
He's putting on an act.

13:02.091 --> 13:07.091
He just chose to save both me and Wales.

13:07.181 --> 13:11.101
He's only feigning madness in order
to take the blame for killing the king.

13:12.311 --> 13:14.641
Let him run wild for a bit.

13:14.731 --> 13:16.311
I'll let you put it to an end.

13:20.021 --> 13:21.271
I don't care.

13:23.191 --> 13:24.401
Thorkell.

13:25.401 --> 13:28.451
I know he's your vassal,

13:28.531 --> 13:31.871
but a dog should be handled by his own master.

13:39.501 --> 13:42.131
What's wrong, Danes?

13:42.211 --> 13:44.131
Askeladd!

13:45.471 --> 13:47.551
You bastard.

13:47.631 --> 13:49.681
Do you have any idea what you've done?

13:49.761 --> 13:51.511
You killed the king.

13:51.601 --> 13:53.931
What are you talking about?

13:54.021 --> 13:56.141
I'm right here, alive and well.

13:57.351 --> 14:00.981
Shut up! You're the child of a slave!

14:02.611 --> 14:03.651
You swine.

14:04.821 --> 14:08.661
Is that how you talk to a king?

14:11.411 --> 14:13.201
Kneel down!

14:13.291 --> 14:16.791
I'll let you have the honor of kissing my shoes

14:16.871 --> 14:18.251
and then die!

14:20.751 --> 14:22.091
Askeladd!

14:24.921 --> 14:26.341
Stay back, Thorfinn!

14:54.621 --> 14:58.661
Is this the first time
you've stabbed someone, prince?

15:07.461 --> 15:08.761
You did well.

15:18.891 --> 15:20.691
Hey, Askeladd.

15:22.151 --> 15:23.981
Hey, that's...

15:24.061 --> 15:26.981
-Did he kill him?
-The prince! The prince did it!

15:37.371 --> 15:38.661
Stand straight.

15:39.661 --> 15:41.411
This part is important.

15:42.831 --> 15:45.381
This moment on stage was created for you.

15:45.461 --> 15:46.881
Don't waste it.

15:50.301 --> 15:54.141
Hey, baldie, what are you doing sleeping there?

15:54.221 --> 15:56.891
Damn. Damn.

15:56.971 --> 16:00.481
How could you let them stab you there, you idiot?

16:00.561 --> 16:02.061
Come on.

16:02.141 --> 16:03.771
Shut up.

16:05.191 --> 16:08.021
Let me rest.

16:08.111 --> 16:11.901
You bastard. Get up. We've got to run away.

16:13.201 --> 16:14.991
You fool.

16:15.071 --> 16:16.951
Just hurry up and do it.

16:17.951 --> 16:19.911
Sorry to make you wait.

16:21.251 --> 16:23.161
I'll give it to you.

16:23.251 --> 16:24.961
I'll give you my life.

16:26.921 --> 16:28.501
Kill me.

16:28.591 --> 16:32.171
We are-- We're enemies after all, right?

16:35.681 --> 16:36.971
Are you going to die?

16:38.641 --> 16:39.721
You?

16:40.721 --> 16:42.811
Hurry up.

16:43.811 --> 16:45.601
There's no time left.

16:50.651 --> 16:53.781
Are you trying to make a fool out of me? You bastard.

16:56.281 --> 16:58.241
It wasn't supposed to be like this!

16:58.321 --> 17:03.581
The duel to settle things between me and you
wasn't supposed to be like this!

17:03.661 --> 17:05.331
I won't forgive you.

17:05.421 --> 17:07.081
Don't die on me.

17:07.171 --> 17:10.591
Get up! Duel me right now!

17:10.671 --> 17:13.841
I'm the one who's supposed to defeat you!

17:13.921 --> 17:15.471
Hey, you!

17:15.551 --> 17:17.841
-You're kidding me! Hurry up and stand!
-Come on.

17:18.851 --> 17:21.101
This is why I hate kids.

17:21.181 --> 17:23.851
Duel me! Hey!

17:26.101 --> 17:27.311
How

17:28.311 --> 17:30.521
do you plan to live your life?

17:34.571 --> 17:36.991
In the future,

17:37.071 --> 17:39.451
after I die,

17:39.531 --> 17:43.041
how do you plan to live your life, Thorfinn?

17:47.371 --> 17:51.131
You haven't thought about it, right?

17:52.381 --> 17:53.961
Shut up.

17:54.051 --> 17:56.551
Move forward already.

17:56.631 --> 17:58.551
Don't stay

18:01.141 --> 18:04.391
stuck in a damn boring place like this forever.

18:05.851 --> 18:09.021
Go far ahead.

18:09.101 --> 18:12.821
Go beyond the world where Thors went.

18:12.901 --> 18:15.781
You're Thors' son. Go.

18:19.031 --> 18:21.031
That's

18:22.491 --> 18:24.491
your real fight.

18:27.541 --> 18:30.381
Become a true warrior,

18:31.631 --> 18:34.211
son of Thors.

19:04.281 --> 19:07.371
Thorfinn, I won't ask you to forgive me.

19:07.451 --> 19:11.001
He was dealt this punishment
because he went mad suddenly

19:11.081 --> 19:14.461
and committed the crime of murdering the king.

19:14.541 --> 19:19.761
However, I'm sure you don't feel like
serving me now that this has happened.

19:20.761 --> 19:22.511
Go wherever you want.

19:40.821 --> 19:41.701
Kill him!

19:41.781 --> 19:44.281
-He's a traitor!
-Stop!

19:44.371 --> 19:45.871
Don't kill him!

19:47.451 --> 19:50.501
Stand back. I will decide what to do with him.

19:52.001 --> 19:54.171
Thorkell, that's enough.

19:56.001 --> 19:59.131
Being stabbed is a small price to pay.

20:00.051 --> 20:03.891
Your Highness, you should have
your wounds treated in the inner chambers.

20:03.971 --> 20:06.931
Let me handle matters here.

20:07.011 --> 20:07.931
Take him.

20:09.851 --> 20:10.851
Floki.

20:12.391 --> 20:14.401
Now that the former king has passed,

20:14.481 --> 20:18.321
do you know who the commander
of the army in England is now?

20:19.481 --> 20:20.991
Well...

20:21.071 --> 20:22.571
What's wrong?

20:22.651 --> 20:23.821
Say it.

20:35.171 --> 20:37.291
Everyone, hear me.

20:38.421 --> 20:39.551
The former king,

20:39.631 --> 20:42.221
His Highness King Sweyn, has passed.

20:42.301 --> 20:44.971
From this day forth, I, Canute,

20:45.051 --> 20:48.511
shall act as the commander of the army
and the ruler of England!

20:52.181 --> 20:54.981
We will not pursue the subjugation of Wales.

20:55.061 --> 20:56.771
Now that the former king has passed,

20:56.851 --> 21:00.361
I predict that the remnants
of the English army will revolt.

21:00.441 --> 21:02.651
We must prepare to handle that first.

21:04.571 --> 21:07.991
I will provide further notice
regarding your rewards later.

21:09.031 --> 21:11.121
That is all. You are dismissed now.

21:19.841 --> 21:21.461
Hey.

21:41.151 --> 21:42.571
Hey.

21:42.651 --> 21:43.821
Hey, you.
